      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# BirdJournal · scene art · tuning\n\nTune the look here, then the batch paints every card with it.\n\n**1 · Picture.** **image 1** is a composite: one of your glasses photos, zoomed 2x to the viewfinder's crop, with the species' reference bird cut out and pasted near the middle at 38 % of the height (`birdjournal-scene-<species>-<garden|lawn|driveway>.png`). The paste happens in Python before ComfyUI (`packbuilder.art.paste_bird`); ask Claude to change the bird's size or placement. Pick another in the dropdown: the samples are the entries starting `birdjournal-` (the same files are in the repo's `samples/` folder), or upload your own.\n\n**2 · Prompt.** Edit the green **prompt template** and **negative prompt**. Words in braces (`{edition_light}`, `{edition_colors}`, `{light}`) are filled from the small field nodes beside it: keep the braces in the template so it goes straight back into `art/prompts.json`, and edit a field's value to try another edition or light. Legendary light, to paste into `{light}`:\n\n> Light it dramatically with a warm golden rim light around the bird, a luminous sky, deep soft shadows and drifting gold motes; the bird keeps its true colours.\n\n**3 · Quality.** **Fast preview** on: the 4-step Lightning LoRA, about 12 s, good for trying wording. Off: full quality (40 steps, cfg 4, about 3.5 min), which paints richer and follows the prompt harder, so judge the style with it off. The seed is fixed on **sampler** so runs compare; change it to see variety.\n\n**4 · Model.** Leave as is: Qwen-Image-Edit-2511 fp8mixed, its text encoder and VAE (all Apache 2.0).\n\n**Run** with Queue (Ctrl+Enter). Paintings land in ComfyUI's `output/birdjournal-tuning/`.\n\n**When you're happy:** turn Fast preview **off**, save (Ctrl+S), and tell Claude. Claude reads this workflow from `user/default/workflows/BirdJournal/`, copies the template, negative prompt and field values into `art/prompts.json` and the graph into `art/workflows/scene-art.json`, and runs the batch. Keep the node titles **image 1**, **prompt**, **negative**, **sampler** and **output**: the batch finds those nodes by title.\n\nWhat the bake-off learned (DECISIONS.md, \"Art model bake-off\"):\n- Naming the species pulls in the model's stereotype of it (a red finch becomes a Northern Cardinal), so scene and photo art never name it.\n- Wording about a 'wilderness quest' replaces the photo's scene with an invented one; keep the photographed moment as the composition.\n- 'Adventure-cover painting' invites the model to letter a title onto the picture. The negative prompt bans text, but it only works with Fast preview **off**: at cfg 1 the negative prompt is ignored."
      ],
      "title": "Read me first",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
